 B  has a lot of its events essentially copy  pasted over from route 8 I could end my  complaint here but that would be a bit  too basic of a qualm to make a whole  video about even though one of the more  common complaints against automata is  precisely this repetition and in defense  of our team one could quickly point to  the different combat styles respect  differences between 9s and to be  presentation of new information in route  P and the different side quests all is  evidence of distinction between routes a  and B and these are all valid points  granted the simplicity of the nine as  hacking can get a bit stale route B does  offer a lot of new information about the  story and world that changes how we see  and understand events that are shared  between the routes the little films  shown before each new zone and 9s his  own revelations as two examples of these  informational differences but I think  everyone could agree that route B is  repetitive to some extent it's an  integral part of the route  it was clearly designed with that  repetition in mind you're supposed to  repeat the events of Rock a but by  gaining better insight and understanding  or up B is supposed to take on its own  form I believe that this repetition has  a very specific purpose  I think Yoko taro and PlatinumGames  wanted this repetition to push the  player into exploring the many side  quests that are only available  throughout B if you're forced to replay  a significant portion of the game you'll  be yearning for something new to do to  combat the monotony and boredom of  replaying content ideally these new side  quests show up and offer the player the  perfect opportunity to rid themselves of  said monotony new missions that reveal  new information and offer new gameplay  scenarios or what people want to see as  they progress through the game and while  the main quest of route B does offer  some new information and insights it's  not quite enough to really get rid of  those negative 